{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_eq_exchange_unit_component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_eq_exchange_unit_component","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L101-L109","doc":"**The amplitude is the exchange component of the unit tangent\n(sorry-free).**  States step 3 explicitly: `ℓ(z)` is the second\n(exchange) coordinate of the unit-normalized channel direction\n`(1, z)/√(1+z²)`.  Together with `ellDirect` and\n`ellDirect_sq_add_ell_sq` this exhibits `(ℓDirect, ℓ)` as a genuine unit\ntangent `(cos θ, sin θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_criticality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_criticality","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L87-L99","doc":"**Deformed criticality (sorry-free).**  At the Markov value `z = 1/w`\n(`w = [2]_v` the loop value) the amplitude lands *exactly* on the\ncriticality locus `ℓ(1/w)²(1+w²) = 1` — the hypothesis of\n`ReebPnMagnitude.ss_det_zero_at_criticality`.  So the derived `ℓ` puts\nthe pn-bond at marginal stability with no free parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_sq_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell_sq_normalization","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**The CWF normalization equation (sorry-free).**  `ℓ(z)²(1+z²) = z²` —\nthe square-root-free content of `ℓ(z) = z/√(1+z²)`, exactly the equation\nthe conjecture `reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.md` states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ellDirect_sq_add_ell_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ellDirect_sq_add_ell_sq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L69-L76","doc":"**Unit tangent (sorry-free).**  The direct and exchange components square\nto `1` — `(cos θ)² + (sin θ)² = 1` — confirming `ℓ` reads a *unit*\ntangent (the CWF normalization, step 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ellDirect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ellDirect","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The **direct (identity-channel) component** of the unit tangent,\n`cos θ = 1/√(1+z²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.ell","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ReebLinkingCWF.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The **CWF linking functional** `ℓ(z) = z/√(1+z²)`: the transverse\n(exchange-channel) component of the unit-normalized channel direction\n`(1, z)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}